  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 5116846080
    m_Localized: 'April 12th

      Today Keita laughed out loud for the first time.

      When
      dad made a funny face, he smiled and reached out.

      I never thought such
      a small thing could make me this happy.

      At night, the three of us bathed
      together, and I fell asleep holding his hand.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25375334400
    m_Localized: 'May 8th

      Today, Miwa from the neighborhood came to visit.
      When I was holding the baby (Keita), she was staring with an envious look that
      was quite striking. When I offered to let her hold Keita, she held him awkwardly,
      like handling fragile goods, but with genuine joy. She also helped with kitchen
      work, which was really helpful.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 32967024640
    m_Localized: 'June 28th

      Today, what Miwa shared with me stayed with me.

      "I
      can''t have children," she said quietly.

      I was surprised and didn''t
      know what to do, so I just hugged her.

      Even though our situations are
      different, I understand the loneliness as a person, so I couldn''t blame her.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 42219659264
    m_Localized: 'July 15th

      Miwa''s face when she held him was very gentle.

      But
      sometimes she says half-jokingly, "If only he were my child..."

      I feel
      my chest tighten, but I just laugh it off.

      I''m grateful to have a friend
      nearby, but I also feel somewhat conflicted.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 48775356416
    m_Localized: 'August 10th

      Keita is definitely my child. Mine and his father''s.

      No
      matter how tired I am, seeing his smile saves me.

      I''m grateful for
      the days I''m supported by having a friend,

      but I still want to cherish
      this child the most.


'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 517333639168
    m_Localized: First Time Parenting Journal
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
